{"title": "Peculiar Flower", "pageid": 47960, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Peculiar_Flower", "categories": ["Environmental objects", "Traps"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:PeculiarFloTrap.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0d/PeculiarFloTrap.png/250px-PeculiarFloTrap.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/0/0d/PeculiarFloTrap.png/375px-PeculiarFloTrap.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/0/0d/PeculiarFloTrap.png 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/0/0d/PeculiarFloTrap.png/250px-PeculiarFloTrap.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/0/0d/PeculiarFloTrap.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>A Peculiar Flower planted (literally) on the ground</figcaption></figure>\n<p>A <b>Peculiar Flower</b> is a unique type of <a href=\"/wiki/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">Trap</a> that might be encountered in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_One\" title=\"Act One\">Act One</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Three\" title=\"Act Three\">Act Three</a> of the game.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Involvement\">Involvement</span></h2>\n<p>A Peculiar Flower is an explosive object, resembling a terracotta-coloured water lily flower having blossomed directly on a hard ground.\n</p><p>These dangerous \"blooms\" will inevitably be encountered by the party if they choose to confront <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Auntie_Ethel\" title=\"Auntie Ethel\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/25px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/38px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/50px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Auntie Ethel\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png/25px-Portrait_Ethel.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/6b/Portrait_Ethel.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Auntie_Ethel\" title=\"Auntie Ethel\">Auntie Ethel</a> either about <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mayrina\" title=\"Mayrina\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/d/de/Portrait_Mayrina.png/25px-Portrait_Mayrina.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/d/de/Portrait_Mayrina.png/38px-Portrait_Mayrina.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/d/de/Portrait_Mayrina.png/50px-Portrait_Mayrina.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Mayrina's\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/d/de/Portrait_Mayrina.png/25px-Portrait_Mayrina.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/d/de/Portrait_Mayrina.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mayrina\" title=\"Mayrina\">Mayrina's</a> fate in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_One\" title=\"Act One\">Act One</a>, or little <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Vanra\" title=\"Vanra\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b0/Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png/25px-Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/b0/Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png/38px-Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/b0/Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png/50px-Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Vanra's\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b0/Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png/25px-Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/b0/Portrait_Vanra_Bergauz.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Vanra\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vanra\">Vanra's</a> fate in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Three\" title=\"Act Three\">Act Three</a>, or both. Lots of them litter the way to the <a href=\"/wiki/Overgrown_Tunnel#Ancient_Abode\" title=\"Overgrown Tunnel\">Ancient Abode</a> through the <a href=\"/wiki/Overgrown_Tunnel\" title=\"Overgrown Tunnel\">Overgrown Tunnel</a> and the antechamber of Ethel's lair in <a href=\"/wiki/The_Blushing_Mermaid\" title=\"The Blushing Mermaid\">The Blushing Mermaid</a>.\n</p><p>Once triggered, a Peculiar Flower deals <span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-fire\">2d6</span>⁠<span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Fire\" title=\"Fire\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/20px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/30px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/40px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Fire\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png/20px-Fire_Damage_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/84/Fire_Damage_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Fire\" title=\"Fire\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-fire\">Fire</span></a> damage via Explosion to any party member who approached it. However, the main danger coming from Peculiar Flowers is that they most often (particularly in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_One\" title=\"Act One\">Act One</a>) are placed in pair with a <a href=\"/wiki/Vent\" title=\"Vent\">Vent</a> emitting a cloud of <a href=\"/wiki/Noxious_Fumes\" title=\"Noxious Fumes\">Noxious Fumes</a>, which are highly flammable. Thus, triggering or failing to disarm a tricky blossom will cause a volume explosion.\n</p><p>Planted Peculiar Flower can be seen on the ground in the plain sight and even through the cloud of Noxious Fumes, but to interact with it a party member must first detect it via passive Perception check.\n</p><p>A Peculiar Flower can be spotted with a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;15 Perception Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;15 <a href=\"/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\">Perception</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a> check and disarmed with the help of <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/25px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/38px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/50px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Sleight of Hand\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png/25px-Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/4/46/Sleight_of_Hand_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\">Sleight of Hand</a> skill, but the interacting party member must have a <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit\" title=\"Trap Disarm Toolkit\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/bf/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Trap_Disarm_Toolkit\" title=\"Trap Disarm Toolkit\">Trap Disarm Toolkit</a> in their inventory. Difficulty Class requirement is a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;10 Sleight of Hand Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;10 <a href=\"/wiki/Sleight_of_Hand\" title=\"Sleight of Hand\">Sleight of Hand</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a> roll.\n</p><p>Also, Peculiar Flowers can be destroyed by shooting or casting <span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-force\"></span>⁠<span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Force\" title=\"Force\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d1/Force_Damage_Icon.png/20px-Force_Damage_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/d/d1/Force_Damage_Icon.png/30px-Force_Damage_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/d/d1/Force_Damage_Icon.png/40px-Force_Damage_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Force\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d1/Force_Damage_Icon.png/20px-Force_Damage_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/d/d1/Force_Damage_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Force\" title=\"Force\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-damage-type-force\">Force</span></a> spells (<span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eldritch_Blast\" title=\"Eldritch Blast\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/d/db/Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp/25px-Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/d/db/Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp/38px-Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/d/db/Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp/50px-Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Eldritch Blast\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/d/db/Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp/25px-Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/d/db/Eldritch_Blast_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Eldritch_Blast\" title=\"Eldritch Blast\">Eldritch Blast</a> confirmed to be effective), although the character must hit the trap almost dead in the center.\n</p><p>After disarming, a Peculiar Flower just disappears in a puff of smoke.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714200954